            <ArticleTitle>Orificial Tuberculosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>120-121</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Two case of orificial tuberculosis had associated diffuse pulmonary tuberculosis. The first case presented as an ulcer on the inner aspect of the right cheek and -the second case presented as a genital ulcer not healing with usual antibodies. He also had an ulcer on the centre of the tongue. The first case was diagnosed as a malignant ulcer and the second case as a venereal ulcer initial. But the investigations proved them to be of tubercular aetiology.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
